# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Smartious Homeschool — Netlify _redirects
# Place this file in the build output (frontend/public/_redirects)
# so Netlify serves it at the site root.
#
# Rules are processed top-to-bottom; first match wins.
#
# TRAILING SLASH HANDLING (one URL per page, no trailing slash):
# scripts/seo-static.mjs writes a FLAT file for every indexable route
# (dist/<route>.html, never dist/<route>/index.html). For a flat file
# Netlify serves /foo at 200 and 301s /foo/ to /foo (Pretty URLs,
# also set in netlify.toml). Slash rules CANNOT be written here:
# Netlify normalises the trailing slash before matching rules, so
# "/foo/ /foo 301" loops (it did — see git history). App-only routes
# served by the SPA fallback are normalised by the inline script at
# the top of index.html.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ─── Home page ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# "/" gets its own static HTML (title, canonical, text and links) written
# by scripts/seo-static.mjs to dist/home.html. index.html stays the plain
# app shell for the SPA fallback below, so other routes never inherit the
# home page's canonical. home.html is always created by the postbuild cp
# step, so this rule can never point at a missing file.
/                        /home.html                  200!

# ─── Retired admissions pages: Book assessment is the only way in ─
/enroll                  /assessment                 301
/consult                 /assessment                 301

# ─── Country hub canonical consolidation (301s) ──────────────────
/us-families             /online-school/usa          301
/ca-families             /online-school/canada       301
/homeschooling-kenya     /online-school/kenya        301
/online-school/uk        /online-school/united-kingdom 301

# ─── Kenya city URL consolidation ────────────────────────────────
# Legacy /homeschooling/<slug> city URLs 301 to the canonical
# /homeschool-<slug> form (matches every other country pattern and
# the URLs Google has already crawled from the Kenya hub cards).
/homeschooling/*         /homeschool-:splat          301

# ─── Renamed documents (the old file names had spaces) ───────────
# Forced (!) because the old files may still exist in public/, and a
# plain rule never fires when a file matches. Both encodings of "(2)".
/Smartious_Company_Portfolio_2026%20(2).pdf      /smartious-portfolio-2026.pdf   301!
/Smartious_Company_Portfolio_2026%20%282%29.pdf  /smartious-portfolio-2026.pdf   301!
/Smartious_Fee_Structure_2026%20(2).pdf          /smartious-fees-2026-27.pdf     301!
/Smartious_Fee_Structure_2026%20%282%29.pdf      /smartious-fees-2026-27.pdf     301!

# ─── Retired demo portal ─────────────────────────────────────────
# The /demo portal was removed; send old links to the home page.
/demo                    /                           301
/demo/*                  /                           301

# ─── SPA fallback — MUST be last so it doesn't override above ────
# Unknown paths render the app's NotFound page (noindex). The portals
# (/admin, /teacher, /student…) also depend on this fallback.
/*                       /index.html                 200
